Хабр, по поводу доставоки посылок с помощью квадрокоптеров

StopDesign:
Думаю, в России скоро запретят дронов вообще. Вот куча аргументов за такой сценарий:
— во-первых, это относительно новая технология, которую нужно запретить просто по привычке;
— во-вторых, дронами можно развозить наркотики, биткойны и детскую порнографию;
— кроме того, армия США использует беспилотники в Ираке (а зачем порядочному гражданину РФ подобная технология?);
— а еще любой китайский n-коптер, конечно же, может использоваться террористами.

en:
Habr, about delivering packages with quadcopters

StopDesign:
I think in Russia they'll ban drones altogether soon. Here are a bunch of arguments for such a scenario:
— first, it's a relatively new technology that needs to be banned just out of habit;
— second, drones can be used to deliver drugs, bitcoins and child porn;
— besides, the US Army uses drones in Iraq (and why would a decent Russian citizen need such a technology?);
— and also any Chinese n-copter can of course be used by terrorists.

from LJ:

The hardest part of the job is the slogan for the ad campaign... It's water after all! Ordinary mineral water. And the slogan options...
For example: "It only has H2O! Nothing more!", "Water — so it rises operationally, the copulatory member right away" "Our water — BonAqua, fuck yeah!", and "I'll drink mineral water and offer everyone oral connections"... And, by the way, the last option was suggested by our deputy director(((

from toster.ru:

ZloyHobbit:
I remember at a hand-to-hand combat seminar someone asked the coach a question: "How do you properly take a perfect punch?". I immediately pictured an absolutely solid fist with mass close to infinite, moving at close to the speed of light, and making an absolutely inelastic contact with the jaw... theoretically the energy released as heat could be enough to destroy a galaxy.

